## What I found and fixed

**The black screen was not 3D.** The intro/title scenes are DS **mode 5 direct-colour affine BGs** (`GX_SetGraphicsMode(1,5,0)` in `ov179/cdemo_main.c:110`; `BG2CNT/BG3CNT = 0x4084/0x4884`). The game loads 256×192 BGR555 frames into VRAM and shows them as 16-bit bitmaps. sinjoh's `g2d` treated every bitmap BG as unsupported, so nothing ever drew. That also explains `kj_g3` commands = 0 and no 3D swaps.

Three concrete defects, all verified:

1. **No quad-arena reset.** The M0 renderer never used the 2D arena, so `kj_gpu_quads_reset()` was missing. After the logo screens the arena filled and every allocation of the intro's 832 cells failed (`unowa_direct_norun == 2` per frame). Fix placed exactly where sinjoh has it (`renderer.c:172`).
2. **Direct-colour BG support.** `affine_bg` hardcoded `bpp8 = true`. It now converts each 8×8 BGR555 cell into an atlas slot with bit 15 as alpha, addressed per NitroSDK `G2_GetBG2ScrPtr` (mode 5: base = `screen_base × 0x4000`, linear rows) and eidos `hwcompose.c:596-660` (`RAS_DIRECT`).
3. **Title animation resources were mis-relocated.** `objTbl[0].anmTbl` (DS `0x021BD3E4`) was rewritten to native `DWCi_FOCUSlInit` because overlay 16 has a function at the same numeric address. `resolve_function` now refuses another overlay's function when the value is inside the current module's own data window; 58 words moved from function pointers to flat data pointers, and the table now rebases correctly.

