  Line 1764:           "text": "This is a very clean game-agnostic bridge. The renderer consumes a coherent DS memory view + decoded G3 frames. The DS side provides: NitroSDK compat, the game code, the G3 display-list interpreter (kj_g3.c), the frame publisher.

The game-specific parts: kj_boot.c (NitroMain entry, cartridge/firmware state setup, file system IDs), data pack (game's file IDs), patches to the game.

kj_g3.c is the DS geometry engine emulation — game-agnostic (it interprets GX FIFO commands).

So for sinjoh, the engine (kohjoh's 3DS side + kj_g3 + compat) can be reused nearly wholesale; the work is:
1. Build pokeplatinum decomp for ARM11 with patches (the biggest chunk).
2. Data pack builder for platinum (file IDs).
3. Game-side patches: boot hook, vblank hook, frame publish hook, save, audio pump, input.
